  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is the current best at 0.527 acc / 0.510 F1, outperforming rna-only (0.485) and far exceeding image-only (0.208). The multiprofile axis is completely untested across all three model settings, representing the largest remaining source of uncertainty. Question: Does aggregating multiple profiles (via avgpool) on top of the best-known multimodal setup yield a meaningful gain over singleprofile? Why this is the best next experiment: config_018 is the minimal, clean extension of the current best (same encoders, same concat fusion) that isolates the multiprofile + avgpool variable. avgpool is chosen over transformer to keep the aggregation simple and reduce overfitting risk with limited data. A positive result would justify investing further in multiprofile configurations (transformer aggregation, other encoders); a null or negative result would efficiently rule out that axis and redirect budget toward image-encoder or RNA-encoder variations. Under a tight budget, resolving this high-impact, unexplored design axis provides the greatest expected information gain per experiment."
}

